<p class="small">The Prospecting Show · Editorial sales resource · Published October 12, 2026 · Updated November 22, 2026</p>
<p>A sales training agenda needs a clear purpose, timed activities, an observable skill, and an owner for follow-through. Use the 30-minute agenda below when a buyer and training provider are deciding what a program should cover. Use the 60-minute agenda when a facilitator is running a practice session with reps.</p>
<p>Both are editable planning templates. The role-play and timing allocations are illustrative, not a tested promise of higher conversion, revenue, or rep performance. Adapt the scope, group size, accessibility, and pace to the participants. The example focuses on asking a factual discovery question and accurately restating the answer.</p>
